{
  "summary": "Resets the request ID and JSON-RPC version fields at the beginning of JSONRPCRequest::parse before validating whether the input payload is an object. This prevents malformed, non-object batch elements from inheriting the ID and version of the preceding element in their error replies.",
  "problem": "During JSON-RPC batch processing, ExecuteHTTPRPC reuses a single JSONRPCRequest instance across all elements. When an element is not a JSON object, parse() throws an invalid request exception before resetting id and m_json_version, causing the error response to reuse the previous request's ID or be dropped entirely if the preceding call was a JSON-RPC 2.0 notification.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'For [{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"getblockcount\",\"id\":\"X\"}, 2] the reply has two objects with \"id\":\"X\", one with a result and one with an error. If the first element is a notification, the error is dropped.'",
    "Functional test in test/functional/interface_rpc.py confirms both failure modes on master and verifies that error replies now have null IDs and are not suppressed following notifications."
  ],
