  "card": "Resets the request ID and JSON-RPC version fields at the start of JSONRPCRequest::parse before verifying whether the input is an object. In JSON-RPC batches, Bitcoin Core reuses a single request instance; non-object elements throw an error before clearing those fields, causing error replies to inherit the prior element's ID or get dropped if the prior call was a notification. The author provides a functional test demonstrating that invalid batch elements duplicate prior IDs and drop notification errors on master, both of which are resolved.",
